Package: com.heavenzy.tweak
Name: Heavenzy
Version: 1.8.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Per-app device identity reset (Blaze-style): keeps your real iPhone model but resets serial, UDID, IDFV, IDFA, Wi-Fi/Bluetooth MAC and IMEI, plus a wipe + re-spoof that clears saved accounts and blocks iCloud restore, so an app sees a brand-new phone with a first-time install. Hold two fingers on any app to open the draggable Kairos panel (touches pass through around it): inside Instagram it scans the visible usernames (Scan, scroll, scan again, Copy). An optional Approved Names list keeps only accounts whose display-name first name matches, and Auto scan taps Scan every second so you just scroll. Close the panel with its X. Each app also has an App Data & Tools screen (AppData-style): view version, build, sizes and containers, open the bundle/data/group folders in Filza, copy the bundle id, clear caches, reset data, reset permissions, offload, or open the App Store page, plus rename the home-screen icon and set a badge count (applied by the SpringBoard hook). Each app also has a Saved Logins screen: snapshot the current logged-in account (data container files, shared app-group containers, keychain items and the spoofed identity) and restore any snapshot later to get straight back into that account - snapshots live outside the app so a wipe or Spoof Chain can't delete them. Settings has an Account screen: sign up or sign in with email + password and every saved login is uploaded to that account and removed from the iPhone; restoring downloads it again, and the same list appears on any phone you sign in on. An account is required: the app shows a sign-in / create-account wall and the tweak stays inactive in every app (no spoofing, no panel, no snapshots) until the Heavenzy app is signed in.
Maintainer: Heavenzy
Author: Heavenzy
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit, com.opa334.libsandy
